<title>USA: HFS files $1.0 bln shelf debt, common.</title>
<headline>HFS files $1.0 bln shelf debt, common.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>HFS Inc, formerly known as Hospitality Franchise Systems Inc, filed Thursday with the Securities and Exchange Commission to offer up to $1.0 billion in debt securities and common stock.</p>
<p>The company said net proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, which may include acqusitions, repayment of debt, working capital and capital expenditures.</p>
<p>The company, which the largest franchisor of hotels and residential real estate brokerage offices, did not name underwriters.</p>
